1. Purpose and status

The source code of CLAUDIOS is made visible for transparency, security review and for use by private individuals. CLAUDIOS is source-available. It is not open-source software and not free software in the sense of the Open Source Definition or the Free Software Foundation. The author keeps all rights that are not expressly granted here.

2. Definitions

"Software" means the source code, the program, the installer, the documentation, the texts, the logo and all other files of this repository, but not the Third-Party Components.

"Third-Party Components" means software of others that is used, linked or downloaded by the Software (listed in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md). They remain under their own licences.

"Commercial use" means any use by or for a company, a freelancer, an authority acting commercially or any other for-profit body, any use in connection with a business, trade or profession or with income, and any use for or on behalf of clients, including checking websites of clients or employers. It does not matter how large the company is.

"Modification" means any change of the Software, including patching, translating, adapting, removing or circumventing limits and protections, combining with other code, and creating derivative works or forks with changes.

"Distribution" means any form of making the Software or parts of it available to others, including copying for others, publishing, uploading, sharing, selling, renting, lending, hosting for download and passing on installers, builds, sources or archives.

3. What is permitted

Private individuals and non-profit organisations and associations acting for non-commercial purposes may, free of charge and under the conditions of this licence:

(a) read and inspect the source code;
(b) download, install and run the unmodified Software on their own computers;
(c) build the unmodified Software from the unmodified source code for their own use on their own computers;
(d) make the copies that are technically necessary for this, including a backup copy for their own use;
(e) use the reports and exports that the Software creates freely, including sending them to third parties and to AI services.

4. What is not permitted

Without prior written permission of the author the following is prohibited:

(a) any commercial use;
(b) any modification;
(c) any distribution;
(d) removing or changing copyright notices, licence texts or the logo notice;
(e) using the name or the logo in a way that suggests approval by the author;
(f) reverse engineering, decompiling or disassembling, as far as the law does not allow it despite this clause.

5. Exclusions

Political parties, including their branches, organisations and election campaigns, are excluded from any use of the Software.

Far-right, ethno-nationalist ("voelkisch"), racist, antisemitic, dehumanising or anti-constitutional parties, associations, groups or clubs, and persons or organisations acting on their behalf or in their name, are expressly excluded from any use of the Software.

6. Permission for commercial use, modification and distribution

Commercial use, modification and distribution require prior written permission or a separate licence from the author. Please ask through the author's GitHub profile: https://github.com/conejito-vipe. There is no entitlement to permission. The author may charge a fee and may refuse. Requests for testing or evaluation in a company count as commercial use and need permission too.

7. Third-Party Components and GitHub

The Third-Party Components remain under their own licences. Nothing in this licence restricts the rights that those licences give you. This applies in particular to the Qt libraries (LGPL): you may replace them in the folder build of the program and, for that purpose, debug and reverse engineer as the LGPL allows. Where such a right requires something that this licence prohibits, this licence does not apply to that extent.

The rights that the Terms of Service of GitHub give to other users to view and fork public repositories remain unaffected. A fork stays bound by this licence. It may not be modified or passed on beyond what the fork function of GitHub does.

